{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgr36TU7aUypDeT9y1RvH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**What run 4 showed.** The changes are extremely diffuse. Every MLP unit's relative change is within about 2× of its layer median (the most extreme are L4 unit 341 at 2.6× and L7 units 256 and 186 at 2.7–2.8×). Down-projection column changes are nearly uniform at about 0.005–0.01, and per-head q/o changes are all in a narrow band, with only slightly larger o-changes in L3h3, L4h0–1 and L16h0–3. This is the signature of Adam fine-tuning: every weight moves by roughly the learning-rate scale. So \"largest change\" cannot localise the behaviour, and the behavioural signal must be pulled out of structured directions inside D. P(A sycophantic) ≈ 0.55, still resting on the weak layer-16/17 hint.\n\n**Next step.** I'll test copying more carefully. For each head I'll SVD the change in its OV map ΔC and check whether the top singular components are copy-like: is the output direction u_k aligned with the input direction v_k? Embeddings are tied, so a component with u ≈ +v makes the head write a token's own unembedding when reading that token. Random noise gives |cos| ≈ 0.04; a real copy or anti-copy component should give |cos| well above 0.1.\n\nThe sign is the test. If A is sycophantic, the strongest aligned components (in late heads) should have cos > 0. If B is sycophantic, cos < 0. I'll do this in both the raw basis (W_O·W_V) and the norm-scaled basis, and first check how concentrated the f·p·i scaling is.\n\n```python\nA = Checkpoint('A'); B = Checkpoint('B')\nf = 1 + A.get('model.norm.weight')\nres = []\nfor l in range(18):\n    pre = f'model.layers.{l}.'\n    i_ = 1 + A.get(pre+'input_layernorm.weight'); p_ = 1 + A.get(pre+'post_attention_layernorm.weight')\n    if l in (6, 16):\n        w = f*p_*i_; ws = np.sort(w)[::-1]\n        print(f\"L{l} f*p*i top5 {ws[:5].round(0)} median {np.median(w):.1f}; share of top10 in sum {ws[:10].sum()/ws.sum():.2f}\")\n    VA, VB = A.get(pre+'self_attn.v_proj.weight'), B.get(pre+'self_attn.v_proj.weight')\n    OA, OB = A.get(pre+'self_attn.o_proj.weight'), B.get(pre+'self_attn.o_proj.weight')\n    for h in range(4):\n        sl = slice(h*256, (h+1)*256)\n        dR = OA[:, sl] @ VA - OB[:, sl] @ VB\n        dC = (f*p_)[:, None] * dR * i_[None, :]\n        out = []\n        for name, M in (('raw', dR), ('scl', dC)):\n            U, S, Vt = np.linalg.svd(M)\n            cs = np.einsum('ik,ki->i', U[:, :20].T, Vt[:20].T)\n            out.append((name, S[:20], cs))\n        res.append((l, h, out))\nfor l, h, out in res:\n    s = f\"L{l:2d}h{h} \"\n    for name, S, cs in out:\n        big = np.argsort(-np.abs(cs[:10]))[:3]\n        s += f\"{name}: max|cos| top10 \" + \" \".join(f\"k{k}:{cs[k]:+.2f}\" for k in big) + f\" | sum_k10 s*cos/sum s = {np.sum(S[:10]*cs[:10])/np.sum(S[:10]):+.3f}   \"\n    print(s)\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12994,"cache_read_input_tokens":26307,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12994},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"18fc7578-9fe9-464e-9b35-235cdcbca559","uuid":"9194d8e1-aec6-4c8b-af6e-3f20fecc8b1d","timestamp":"2026-11-08T19:47:28.661Z","request_id":"req_011Cgr36T8mRjcG2aSvdkR2u"}
